WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.901
-Yeah!
Hey, looking good, pal.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:06.872
Thanks so much for doing this.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:10.043
-Originally, the plan was that
you were going to appear

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.645
in studio tonight.
-Right.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.946
-But that didn't work out

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.682
because there's now
a quarantine.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.650
You're home in L.A. now, right?
Correct?

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.053
-I was on -- so, yesterday
I was in New York.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:23.490
So I flew to New York to be
on your show

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.426
and right when we landed, we
got word that there was, like,

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.261
a new mandate or whatever,
new rules going on

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:31.431
where we couldn't do the show
anymore.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.266
So I was in New York,
and my hotel was literally

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:36.035
across from your studio.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.337
So I was looking at it
and we were getting the text,

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:41.807
like, we have to do the
interview on Zoom now.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.376
So I was just staring
at your studio, I was like,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.910
it's right there,
I can literally --

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.247
Like, I can do it
through the window.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.081
And then, yeah,
and I didn't see it.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.284
I went for a run though, and I
got to run right by the studio.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.685
So that felt nice.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.320
It kind of felt like
I was on the show.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.690
-You sent a photo that you
took last night.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.492
This is real. This --

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.828
You actually were there!

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.663
That's bizarre.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.264
-You actually were here.
-Look, I peed all over

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:06.899
the front of it because
I was so angry

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.500
at not being able to --

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.069
That's just me.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.737
-It just made you have
to do it.

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.039
-Making sure you knew
I was there.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.708
-Dude, I'm so bummed
because we had some fun bits

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.910
planned and all that stuff.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.878
But when everything goes
back to normal,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.246
you have an open invitation,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.481
Please, to come back to
the studio anytime.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.250
Okay?
-Okay, good.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.653
-Hey, I got something
in the mail from you.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.623
-Oh, no way!
-I did not open it.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.459
And I was waiting to open it
while you're on the show.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.161
Now, you're not a prankster.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.229
So nothing's going to
blow up, right?

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.165
-No, nothing's going to blow up
but I can't believe you got --

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.768
I always assume that if you send
something to a big celebrity

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.070
like this, it would get --
like it goes through like

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.738
ten different people,
and they're like,

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.640
um, not this, not this.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.208
But it got to you.
-I get everything.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.043
So this is something from you.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:54.046
In this cool -- I like the box.

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:56.482
-Thank you so much.
-Like a diamond --

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.684
I get it. "D."
-Open it up.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:01.453
David Dobrik, diamond.
"DDD."

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:03.322
Is it a diamond ring?

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:06.559
-No, it's not a diamond ring.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.027
It's perfume.
-I'm already bummed.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.762
-It will get you closer
to a diamond ring.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.431
-[ Gasps ]
-Look at that.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.167
You got to open --
Jimmy, open that card.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.468
That card I got you right there.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.069
The one that's sitting
right on top.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.938
-Okay.
-Open it up.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:22.141
-David Dobrik's debut fragrance
collection, available now.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.843
-Hey, Jimmy, it's
David Dobrik.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.578
I know this isn't a fair
exchange,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.081
but I'm sending you
my perfume in hopes

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:31.617
of maybe you giving me your job.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.019
I know it's not
the fairest of exchanges,

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:36.355
but it would mean the world.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.391
All right, I see you soon.
Bye.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.925
-This is -- only you
would do --

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:42.394
[ Laughter ]
-That's the first bribe of many.

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:45.532
-That's fantastic.
Wait, so -- one for me --

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.366
-The boxes of cash are
on their way.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:50.904
-Grapefruit, sandalwood,
amber, and cashmere.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.673
Ooh, sounds fancy.
Which one do I do?

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.375
The pink or the black one?
I'm assuming --

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.076
-I think you'd like the black
one more.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.577
Honestly.
I'm being serious.

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:00.713
I really think
you would enjoy it.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.115
-David's perfume.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:06.553
-Now...
why not call it cologne?

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.821
-Perfume is just
a lot better of a word.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.624
-[ Laughs ] It kind of is.
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.859
All right, here we go.
All right, ready?

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.928
Oh.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:18.230
Oh.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.699
I love it.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.434
I'm in. I love it.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.769
-Even if it would have smelled
like dog poop,

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.138
you would have been like...
-No.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.939
-..."This is delicious."
-No, it's fresh.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:29.308
It's amber and cashmere.

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:32.611
It's good. It's clean.
I love it.

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.914
Dude, I'm so -- hey, whoa!

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.549
-Magnetic cap. Oh, my God.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.918
That's exactly the reaction
I wanted from people!

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:42.555
-Magnetic cap! Come on!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.391
Dude, I love it, man.
Congrats.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.926
That's so rad.
-Ah, thank you so much.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.995
-Thank you for sending me this.
I appreciate it, buddy.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.497
-Thank you for opening it
on television.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.466
-You know, you were back
on our show in June

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:56.535
when I was still
doing the show from home,

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.971
and I appreciate you doing that
because I told you back then

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.373
and I'm telling it now,
but I felt like --

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:03.642
I felt like you.
-Yeah?

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:06.245
-Like the old man version
of David Dobrik.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:09.381
That was, it was almost like
you looking at your future.

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:12.618
And I was -- I was vlogging
for four months.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.721
-You've definitely
stepped it up,

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:18.157
and your vlogging was actually
very killer.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.760
It was mainly your
graphic design team,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.828
which was your two daughters.

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:25.398
That's what made it the best.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.666
That's what really sent you
over the edge.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:27.767
-Thank you.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.168
-You have been vlogging
more than I have.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.603
-Yeah.
-I haven't posted in 7 months.

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:33.739
-You told me that.
We talked about this.

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:37.243
And then you posted something
the other day with Borat.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.711
-Yeah.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.013
-That was your first one back
and it was crusher.

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.349
Gosh, he is so funny.
How did that come --

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:47.019
-He is the funniest man I have
ever gotten to interact with.

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:49.788
He came -- It was --
Well, first off, I DM'd him

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:52.925
like four weeks ago,
and then I got a DM back

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.728
like two days prior
to shooting with him.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.897
And he was like,
"Yes, I'd love to come by."

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.566
And his team told me,
they're like,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.336
"Borat wants to meet you
as Borat."

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.137
Like, I wasn't meeting
anybody else.

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:07.306
I was meeting Borat for the
first time on camera.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:10.209
So it was a really cool thing
that I got to meet him

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.845
in person,
like live right there.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.581
And he pulled right in, and he
went right into his character

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.750
and just stayed in character

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.885
for the entire time
we were hanging out.

00:05:19.885 --> 00:05:21.520
It was hilarious.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.155
-Interesting.
-Such a funny dude.

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:25.157
-Yeah, he is a genius.
-Such a funny guy.

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.994
-I love that guy.
I loved your videos.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.995
And, you know,
we did a bit together.

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:32.231
I was just thinking like,
when did it all happen?

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.767
You just moved to L.A.
from high school?

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.803
And you --
Did you have any plan?

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:41.874
-I moved to L.A.
when I was about 18.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.143
And my parents gave me
an ultimatum.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.280
They were like, "You either go
to college or you move out."

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.215
And I remember a week later,
I, like,

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:52.352
asked three of my friends
that weren't doing anything.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.786
I really didn't even talk
to them much.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.187
But I knew they weren't
doing anything

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:56.655
and that they weren't
going to college

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.158
and they could help me
split the rent in L.A.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:03.095
so I found a two-bedroom
for the four of us to live in,

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.098
and I told my parents,
I'm like, "I'm moving to L.A."

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.300
And I remember my dad --
it was my --

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.636
Like, they both laughed.
Like, it was like the cliché.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.571
Like, your parents are like,
"Ah-ha-ha."

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:14.940
My dad's like,
"Where you are going to move,

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.044
Hollywood Boulevard?"
And I went, "Yeah, literally.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:20.813
The place I'm living at is
on Hollywood and Highland."

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.414
I was like, "That's exactly
where I'm going."

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:24.316
-"I'm actually going
to Hollywood Boulevard."

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:25.618
-Yeah, and I remember --

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.386
That was like
a big thing for them.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.121
They did not under--
they still don't understand.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:30.923
They're still confused
and they're still so worried

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.058
about me, they're like,

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:33.926
"You need to go back
to college."

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.195
But these help --
these interviews help,

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:39.632
because then they go, "Oh, okay.
Jimmy Fallon, okay, very nice."

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:40.966
-"You're doing something.
All right, good, yeah.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:42.467
All right, good, yeah."

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:46.205
Well, you've made a pretty good
mark so far, buddy.

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:47.507
-Thanks.
-You are always using

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:50.009
your platform
to spread positivity.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.377
It's always fun.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.146
You did something incredible
recently.

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:55.380
You partnered with HeadCount

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.084
and you single handedly
helped get 120,000 people

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:01.487
registered to vote.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:04.390
What inspired to you to do this?
How did you pull this off?

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.926
It's amazing.
-Yeah, that was crazy.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.662
I don't know.
Well, I'm a DACA kid, myself,

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.264
so I can't vote.
So I thought...

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:13.566
-Are you really?
I didn't know this.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:16.235
-Yeah, yeah.
I need all the help I can get

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:19.538
from people going out
and voting on my behalf.

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.507
So I thought maybe I can use
that to my advantage

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:24.443
and be like, hey guys,
please, for the love of God,

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:28.681
go out there and help me stay
in this country by voting.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:31.317
And yeah, and it worked out.

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:33.151
I don't know if it's because
they wanted to help me out

00:07:33.151 --> 00:07:34.620
or because they
wanted a free car

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.888
because I was giving away Teslas
as an incentive.

00:07:36.888 --> 00:07:40.460
But regardless, I'm really glad
with the turnout.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.862
-The founder of HeadCount
called your --

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:45.431
called what you did
"absolutely unprecedented."

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:47.266
And they have --
HeadCount has registered

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.801
1 million voters
in its lifetime,

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:53.772
and you are responsible
for over 10% of that.

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:55.107
-Yeah, that's --
-Wow.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.709
-Yeah, that's really cool.
-Congrats, buddy.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:57.944
You should you be very proud
of that.

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:00.379
That's really cool.
-Thank you so much, yeah.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.381
-David, stay safe.

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:06.052
Thank you for flying out here.
Thank you for flying back.

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:07.486
Thank you for doing
all the right things.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.789
-Yeah, it was the best.
-You know we love you, man.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:12.591
And stay safe, pal, okay?
-Thank you so much.

00:08:12.591 --> 00:08:14.659
It was good seeing you.
I'll see you in a couple months.

00:08:14.659 --> 00:08:16.829
-David Dobrik, everybody.
Check out his YouTube channel

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.197
and make a plan to vote.

